description:
One identification in the shape the official ShieldLabs server SDKs return, whether it was read
from the History API or received in an `identification.scored` webhook. Field names follow the
webhook `data` object. Conversion rules from a History row:
- `user_hid`: an empty string becomes `null`; `anonymous` and the other markers stay strings;
- `domain`: `site_domain` when present, otherwise `domain`;
- `public_ip`: `ip` (`0.0.0.0` becomes `""`) and `country`;
- `local_ip`: `webrtc_leak_ip` and `webrtc_leak_country` when `webrtc_leak_source` is set and not
  `none`, otherwise `web_rtc_ip` and `web_rtc_country` (`0.0.0.0` becomes `""`);
- `traffic_source`: `traffic_channel`, `referrer_domain`, `entry_url`, `click_id_type` and the
  `utm_*` fields, `""` when omitted;
- `risk_score`: `score`;
- `signals`: the `score_details` entries with a non-zero `Value`, in order, each with a signal
  name derived from its description, the weight and the original description;
- `detection_flags`: the `is_*` columns and `check_incomplete`; `browser_vpn_proxy` is
  `connection_type == "browser_vpn_proxy"`; `ip_mismatch` is true (except for search-engine
  crawlers) when a score detail starts with `IP ≠ leakIP` or when the public and the local IP
  are both known and differ; `suspicious_paid_click` is `false` when omitted;
- `observed_at`: `created_at` read as UTC.

From a webhook, the fields are copied; a missing detection flag is `false` and `description` of
every signal is `null`. In JSON, `observed_at` is RFC 3339 in UTC with millisecond precision
(truncated, never rounded).

ConnectionType.description:
How the visitor connected. Known values:
- `direct`: a regular connection;
- `mobile`: a mobile carrier network;
- `vpn`: a VPN;
- `proxy`: a proxy, datacenter or hosting network (search-engine crawlers are reported here too);
- `tor`: the Tor network;
- `privacy_relay`: a privacy relay such as iCloud Private Relay;
- `browser_vpn_proxy`: a VPN or proxy built into the browser or one of its extensions;
- `unknown`: not enough data.

The value can say `vpn` while `detection_flags.vpn` is `false` (IP intelligence classified the
network, but the scored VPN check did not fire). Branch on `detection_flags` for decisions.
The set is open: keep values added in later versions and treat them as `unknown`.
